# "hello, this is a test" for Allison, hand-written.
#
#   ceps-dump C:\tmp\ceps\Allison speak examples\hello.score out.wav
#
# f0   <time_s> <hz>          point on the F0 contour
# unit <type|#index> <end_s> [rescale]
#
# `end_s` is the segment end time; it becomes target_end in samples, so the
# gaps between consecutive units are the durations.
#
# IMPORTANT: keep the contour near the voice's own recorded F0. Allison sits at
# roughly 250-280 Hz. concat_units does not resample -- add_residual centre-pads
# with zeros -- so asking for 185 Hz here stretches every period by 1.4x and
# makes 29% of the excitation silence, which buzzes badly. Check the
# "inserted silence" figure the CLI prints; under ~5% is healthy.
#
# The real engine escapes this constraint through unit selection: f0_weight in
# the join cost pulls in candidates whose recorded F0 is already near the
# target, so it can reach 150 Hz without stretching anything. Until selection
# lands, stay inside the voice's natural range.

lead_f0 270

f0 0.00 272
f0 0.35 278
f0 0.80 262
f0 1.30 250
f0 1.90 240

unit paustart  0.08
unit heh       0.20
unit eh1       0.34
unit low       0.44
unit ow1       0.62
unit paumid    0.70

unit dih       0.80
unit ih1       0.88
unit s         0.98
unit ih0       1.05
unit z         1.14
unit ah0       1.22

unit teh       1.34
unit eh1       1.48
unit s         1.60
unit t         1.70
unit pauend    1.90
